  "title": "The theorem favors no particular state theory",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "280f2a51-1461-4460-97c8-f680732fcc24",
      "text": "The theorem does not pick a state theory. It asks only that an attribution be uniquely determined by $X_t$, invariant under changes of description, and able to produce a causal effect, and leaves open which property of the present state constitutes experience.",
